## Why This Is Asked

This question evaluates practical implementation of multi-tenant isolation in analytics environments, specifically testing knowledge of data-layer controls, IAM scoping, performance optimization, and automated validation mechanisms. It demonstrates understanding of defense-in-depth principles in shared cloud resources.

## Key Concepts

- BigQuery isolation patterns: per-tenant datasets vs. Row-Level Security
- Authorized views and security policy implementation
- IAM role-based access controls with least privilege
- CI/CD validation using synthetic tenant simulation
- Performance optimization with per-tenant BI Engine reservations

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo CI script sketch for synthetic tenant validation
const validateTenantIsolation = async () => {
  // Provision synthetic tenant
  await createSyntheticTenant();
  // Test cross-tenant access attempts
  await attemptCrossTenantQueries();
  // Validate isolation enforcement
  await verifyAccessControls();
  // Rollback on failure
  if (!isolationValidated) await rollback();
};
```

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design cryptographic isolation and operational controls for multi-tenant data in GCP. Assesses understanding of CMKs, envelope encryption, and how to integrate rotation, access policies, and automated validation into CI/CD to prevent data leakage and enable safe rollback.

## Key Concepts

- Customer-managed keys (CMKs) in Cloud KMS
- Envelope encryption for DB and object storage
- IAM Conditions and tenant-scoped service accounts
- Key rotation and versioning
- CI/CD validation and synthetic-tenant rollback

## Code Example

```javascript
// Encrypt with Cloud KMS (example)
const {KeyManagementServiceClient} = require("@google-cloud/kms");
const client = new KeyManagementServiceClient();
async function encrypt(plaintext, name) {
  const [result] = await client.encrypt({name, plaintext: Buffer.from(plaintext)});
  return result.ciphertext;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you audit and detect misconfigurations in KMS IAM Conditions and CMK bindings?
- What are the trade-offs of per-tenant CMKs vs centralized keys, and how would you mitigate overhead with automation?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests the ability to apply concrete Google Cloud controls for multi-tenant isolation at runtime, beyond theoretical concepts, with a practical path from IAM to data and storage gates.

## Key Concepts

- IAM Conditions for per-tenant API access
- Storage prefixes and signed URLs for per-tenant data
- Per-tenant logging/alerting for exfiltration attempts
- CI gates that detect misconfig and roll back changes

## Code Example

```javascript
// Simple tenant check in API middleware
function authorize(req, res, next) {
  const tenantFromToken = req.user?.tenantId;
  const requestedTenant = req.params.tenantId;
  if (tenantFromToken !== requestedTenant) return res.status(403).send('Forbidden');
  next();
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test the CI gate if a misconfig slips through?
- What are trade-offs of per-tenant prefixes vs separate buckets for storage isolation?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests on-demand, auditable access in a shared GCP workspace, ensuring least privilege and robust revocation.

## Key Concepts

- IAM Conditions

- Access Context Manager

- VPC Service Controls

- Auditability and synthetic validation

## Code Example

```javascript
// Example policy binding (pseudo)
{
  \"bindings\": [
    {
      \"role\": \"roles/bigquery.dataViewer\",
      \"members\": [\"serviceAccount:auditor@example.iam.gserviceaccount.com\"],
      \"condition\": {
        \"title\": \"tenantScope\",
        \"expression\": \"resource.name.startsWith('projects/tenant-123/datasets/tenant_123_') && request.time < timestamp('2026-12-01T00:00:00Z')\"
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you handle multiple concurrent audits?
- How do you prove no cross-tenant access occurred during expiry?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests end-to-end thinking for tenant-scoped data retention across multiple services with auditability and rollback capabilities.

## Key Concepts

- Data tagging and lineage across Storage, BigQuery, and Pub/Sub
- Tenant-scoped retention policies, TTLs, and legal holds
- IAM Conditions, per-tenant service accounts, and KMS constraints
- Immutable logs and cryptographic attestations for verification
- Rollback procedures and audit verification planning

